{
  "borough": "Harrow",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Approved",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development hereby permitted shall be begun before the expiration of three years from the date of this permission.",
    "&lt;p&gt;The larger HMO hereby permitted shall not be occupied by more than eight persons at any given time, unless otherwise agreed and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority.&lt;/p&gt;",
    "The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans and documents:&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height: 115%;&quot;&gt;Design\r\nand Access Statement, Reasonable Exception Statement, Site Location Plan, DRG.\r\nNo. 01, 02, 03, 04, 05, 06&lt;/span&gt;",
    "&lt;p class=&quot;MsoListParagraph&quot;&gt;Notwithstanding\r\nthe approved details, within 3 months of the date of this consent, revised\r\ndetails of sufficient bin storage for the development (8 person HMO) containing\r\nspace for a minimum of 4 x 240L wheelie bins (2 x Household Waste and 2 x\r\nRecycling Waste), 4 x 23L individual food waste bins and space for the option\r\nof a 1 x 240L garden waste wheelie bin, shall be submitted to for approval in\r\nwriting by the Local Planning Authority. The bin storage shall be implemented\r\nin accordance with the approved details within 1 month of the approval. The\r\nrefuse and waste bins shall be stored at all times, other than on collections\r\ndays, within the designated refuse storage areas as shown on the approved\r\nplans.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;\r\n\r\n&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;MsoListParagraph&quot;&gt;REASON:\r\nTo ensure adequate bin storage facilities for the development.&lt;font face=&quot;Arial, sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;&quot;&gt;Notwithstanding\r\nthe approved details, within 3 months of the date of this consent, revised\r\ndetails of secure shelters, racks, dimensions and location of cycle parking\r\nspaces shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning\r\nauthority. The cycle storage shall be made available prior to occupation and\r\nshall be retained thereafter.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n\r\n&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;&quot;&gt;NOTE:&amp;nbsp; Cycles parking spaces should be secure and\r\nsheltered.&amp;nbsp; LB Harrow do not support the\r\nprovision of vertical cycle storage systems as this excludes less able people\r\nfrom being able to securely store their cycle.&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n\r\n&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;\r\n\r\n&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;&quot;&gt;REASON:\r\nTo ensure the satisfactory provision of revised safe cycle storage facilities,\r\nto provide facilities for all the users of the site and in the interests of\r\nhighway safety and sustainable transport, in accordance with policy T5 of The\r\nLondon Plan (2021) and policy DM42 of the Harrow Development Management\r\nPolicies Local Plan (2013).&lt;font face=&quot;Arial, sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;line-height: 107%;&quot;&gt;Evidence of certification of Secure by\r\nDesign Accreditation for the development shall be submitted within 3 months of\r\nthe date of this permission, to the Local Planning Authority for approval in\r\nwriting. The development shall only be operated in accordance with the\r\napproval.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;&quot;&gt;REASON: In the interests of creating\r\nsafer and more sustainable communities and to safeguard amenity by reducing the\r\nrisk of crime and the fear of crime. the Local Plan (2013), and Section 17 of\r\nthe Crime &amp;amp; Disorder Act 1998.&lt;font face=&quot;Arial, sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
